{"title":"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(Quick_Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3(Quick Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By a proper <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisor\" title=\"Divisor\">divisor</a> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Natural_number\" title=\"Natural number\">natural number</a> we mean a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Positive\">positive</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integral</a> divisor other than 1 and the number itself. A natural number greater than 1 will be called <i>nice</i> if it is equal to the product of its distinct proper divisors. What is the sum of the first ten nice numbers?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75dfcf7177739e768582307df28f20b900dab55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> denote the product of the distinct proper divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. A number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <i>nice</i> in one of two instances: \n</p>\n<ol><li>It has exactly two distinct <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Prime\">prime</a> divisors.\n<dl><dd>If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f013a72571040ea23962d475f73b6855e074bd1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = pq$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"11\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f779d95c15f7e41de74cb767f52fe4e7b92c745e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> are the prime factors, then its proper divisors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/e/38e6d112c3db52275f5aa750089cc57a05dd336c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n) = p \\cdot q = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />.</dd></dl></li>\n<li>It is the cube of a prime number.\n<dl><dd>If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/2799c1e92e623a15eeac4cfac16e484644793129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=p^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> prime, then its proper divisors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591f689f950feb4a9cff58ff3166d915f916a405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/2/6d2eb4988a6731c6217eaaf1f3969d137c829d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n) = p \\cdot p^2 =n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"19\" />.</dd></dl></li></ol>\n<p>We now show that the above are the only two cases. Suppose that another nice number existed that does not fall into one of these two categories. Then we can either express it in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/428d854a61771c8934ab860702e28bf384524075.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = pqr$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"11\" /> (with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f779d95c15f7e41de74cb767f52fe4e7b92c745e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> prime and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b4e485bf802fab7cae595eefd961523b68ffc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />) or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/268fa20c207168aa7ca356563297eb2b8822444e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = p^e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" /> (with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a8400c2f3f0dc84d3205cacf6b8f20dd1f596650.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e \\neq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" />). \nIn the former case, it suffices to note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf6c578d44d1215af0a0b7ddf1286b30ae95a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n) \\ge (pr) \\cdot (qr) = pqr^2 &gt; pqr = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"280\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>In the latter case, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3356d79bf8a91a341ee2f3ed88505354028ccb8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n) = p \\cdot p^2 \\cdots p^{(e-1)} = p^{(e-1)e/2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/3/103fcd537d8b2db2fe6dc52eb3bed1d8b74d7792.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(n) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6008fb72ccdf2f80f1cdcbb8e824b9589cb53b4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^{(e-1)e/2} = p^e \\Longrightarrow e^2 - e = 2e \\Longrightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"266\" height=\"19\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3e5392cab9c310a66859fefbc5d5c84b93c9c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/6/4a66332dcde07a7f80f49ae1b54b8970bbaf0130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e = 3$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />.  \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a8400c2f3f0dc84d3205cacf6b8f20dd1f596650.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e \\neq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" />, in the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96cab8f363e9195fb9fc18d0274da9e35e907a70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e = 0 \\Longrightarrow n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"124\" height=\"13\" /> does not work. \n</p><p>Thus, listing out the first ten numbers to fit this form, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/8/218dd232f8d6d0448198bb6018654b0df5cae17c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 3 = 6,\\ 2^3 = 8,\\ 2 \\cdot 5 = 10,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"219\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d1becd53802bdd9a1b870648e6bcfe0dcedbeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ 2 \\cdot 7 = 14,\\ 3 \\cdot 5 = 15,\\ 3 \\cdot 7 = 21,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"258\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a6964f4ca9949c1e63509c06ccf1010fdafc4f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ 2 \\cdot 11 = 22,\\ 2 \\cdot 13 = 26,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"188\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00c2c0aa12872df0f3971c07cbf950a07b5efba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ 3^3 = 27,\\ 3 \\cdot 11 = 33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sum\" title=\"Sum\">Summing</a> these yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dce34b2dd732171a566921f8f38c77e63d8696e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{182}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alternatively, we could note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is only nice when it only has two proper divisors, which, when multiplied, clearly yield <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. We know that when the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime_factorization\" title=\"Prime factorization\">prime factorization</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c6cf0cf36da9f62e5085d0f66b50d1d92207109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = a_1^{b_1} \\cdot a_2^{b_2} \\cdot a_3^{b_3} . . . \\cdot a_m^{b_m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"183\" height=\"20\" />, the number of factors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594842eefd041b90b748b3913d652f567078482a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n) = (b_1 + 1)(b_2 +1)(b_3 +1) . . . (b_m +1).\\]\" width=\"326\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is nice, it may only have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factors (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />). This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/a/6da7479b9407d3e82fdcf9c5085ed5577b27c894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />. The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can only be factored into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/9201e5ff959706e138d76a0875e2b8293fde3872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d50a6e8fa45e9036a9bcf109b6044749ce65843d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4)(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" />, which means that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/7/ad79bea94962f7b6a51157fd8465a31a32eb4b7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec8f7a031ab28e48e8c67eca9fb7f6901f54faad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/320cd1ba1cbf20e8c03878bcebc24c4b50870f02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore the only two cases are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f013a72571040ea23962d475f73b6855e074bd1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = pq$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"11\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d510af1b40a36bf15be2381233970315c40f5a5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = p^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />.\nAnd then continue.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3.28Quick_Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(Quick_Brute_Force)\">Solution 3(Quick Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3(Quick Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The only numbers that are \"nice\" will contain four factors, including one and itself. The other two are a \"factor pair\", which, when multiplied, give the original number. Testing for \"nice\" numbers, we get:\n6, 8, 10, 14, 15, 21, 22, 26, 27, and 33.\nAdding them up gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dce34b2dd732171a566921f8f38c77e63d8696e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{182}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />. ~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME\" title=\"1987 AIME\">1987 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1987 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1987\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017180205\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.070 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 351/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9646/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.392      1 -total\n 60.53%    8.106      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.01%    4.956      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2830:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017180205 and revision id 285032. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}